     1	# ROUTER.md
     2	
     3	> ## 🛑 Before you build anything: check whether it already exists.
     4	>
     5	> This repo's most expensive recurring defect is **re-inventing a subsystem that is already
     6	> here** — not writing bad code. It has happened repeatedly, to humans and agents alike, and
     7	> reading this sentence is not enough to prevent it. **Run these four checks; they take under a
     8	> minute and each one has caught a real duplicate:**
     9	>
    10	> 1. `gh pr list -R HiQS-Suite/rebalanceOS` **and** `gh pr list -R Hypercart-Dev-Tools/rebalance-OS`
    11	>    — work in flight is invisible to a code search. An entire `rebalance/lib/*_ops` consolidation
    12	>    campaign was resumed from scratch in 2026-08 because its remaining phases were sitting in
    13	>    unmerged PRs on the *other* repo.
    14	> 2. **The roadmap ledger's "In progress" rows** (`python3 utils/py/releases_app.py roadmap list`) — the campaigns already under way. `utils/pdda/prior-art-check.sh` reads them from `releases.db`.
    15	> 3. **`grep -rn "<the concept>" --include="*.py" .` across `src/`, `utils/`, `HiQS/`** — a helper
    16	>    you are about to write may exist in a package you were not looking at. A clean-room import
    17	>    gate (`HiQS/tests/test_clean_room.py`) was duplicated in 2026-08 by someone who never looked
    18	>    in `HiQS/`.
    19	> 4. **Run the full suite, including the parts CI skips** — `pytest tests/ HiQS/tests`
    20	>    (note: `utils/3-eyes/tests` is deferred per `AGENTS.md`). A test that exists but never runs
    21	>    will not tell you it already covers your idea.
    22	>
    23	> If a thing exists and is inadequate, PDDA Phase 0 requires you to state **why extending it does
    24	> not work** before replacing it. "I did not know it was there" is the failure this block exists
    25	> to stop, and it is not a reason.
    26	
    27	This file is the first entry point for an AI agent working in this repo: it tells you what to read, what to run, and which files are canonical. **This repo is an MCP server** — reach for the MCP tools before scanning code or writing ad-hoc shell pipelines.
    28	
    29	## Role split
    30	
    31	- `ROUTER.md` = startup order and canonical entry points (this file)
    32	- `AGENTS.md` = behavioral rules, the MCP tool surface, the onboarding flow, and decision quality
    33	- `ARCHITECTURE.md` = system orientation (Signal Sources, Source→Table fanout, "Adding a New Source") — read at session start
    34	- `GUIDING-PRINCIPLES.md` = the *why* behind architecture and design decisions; includes the AI doc-review heuristics appendix
    35	- `README.md` = human-facing repo/product overview and install path
    36	- `CLAUDE.md` = the Claude Code entry stub; it defers to `AGENTS.md` for all behavioral rules
    37	- `releases.db` (dumped to `releases.sql`) = the work ledger of in-progress, queued, completed, attempted, and deferred work — read with `releases_app.py roadmap list`, write only with `roadmap add|update|move|rate|repoint`. `ROADMAP.md` was retired in GH-348 (`.pdda-mode` carries `ROADMAP_SOURCE=releases`); do not recreate it.
    38	- `CHANGELOG.md` = the end-of-iteration running log
    39	- `RELEASES.md` = forward-looking release-planning ledger (governed by `PROJECT/PDDA.md`)
    40	- `PROJECT/**` docs = canonical execution detail for a specific effort
    41	- `PROJECT/PDDA.md` = document contract and PDDA automation rules
    42	
    43	## Startup sequence
    44	
    45	1. Read `ROUTER.md` to understand the repo's operating order and canonical files. -> expect one clear next file, not a repo-wide scavenger hunt.
    46	2. Read `AGENTS.md` before making recommendations or edits. -> expect the MCP tool surface, the onboarding flow, explicit assumptions, and verified-claims-only discipline.
    47	3. Read `ARCHITECTURE.md` for orientation, then `src/rebalance/ingest/index_ops.py` — the `COLLECTORS` registry is the data-plane spine. -> expect to extend a source with one `register_collector(...)` call, not edits to the dispatch chain.
    48	4. Run `python3 utils/py/releases_app.py roadmap list` to find the active effort or parked intake. -> expect each row to link outward to its canonical `PROJECT/**` doc; the ledger is a pointer index, not a plan body.
    49	5. Read the linked `PROJECT/**` document that owns the work you are touching. -> expect a near-top `## Status` table telling you what was just completed and what is next.
    50	6. If the task touches project docs, read `PROJECT/PDDA.md` and follow the PDDA contract. -> expect `PROJECT/2-WORKING` docs to have frontmatter, the exact status table, and QA gates when phased.
    51	7. Before reporting success on code or runtime work, run `rebalance doctor` and `pytest tests/`. -> expect doctor clean and the suite green; do not claim completion if either fails or was skipped.
    52	8. Before reporting success on doc-hygiene or roadmap work, run `utils/pdda/pdda.sh run` (or the relevant `utils/pdda/pdda.sh <check>` command). -> expect deterministic findings first, then any LLM review.
    53	
    54	## Canonical rules
    55	
    56	- This repo **is** an MCP server. Use the MCP tools (`index_status`, `refresh_index`, `semantic_query`, …) for data refresh and retrieval, and `rebalance doctor` for setup/health. Do not write ad-hoc `rebalance ...` shell pipelines or grep for setup scripts.
    57	- Do not put phase checklists, build steps, or deep execution notes in roadmap ledger rows.
    58	- Every active doc in `PROJECT/2-WORKING/` must be reflected by a roadmap ledger row that links it (`roadmap repoint`/`update`/`move` when a capture is promoted) — or opt out with `roadmap_exempt: true` in its frontmatter. Enforced by `utils/pdda/pdda.sh roadmap-coverage`; governance lives in `PROJECT/PDDA.md`.
    59	- Every captured GitHub issue doc in `PROJECT/1-INBOX/GH-*.md` is first-class intake and must also be parked as a queue row immediately at capture — `python3 utils/py/releases_app.py roadmap add --issue-num N --issue-url U --title T --created YYYY-MM-DD --doc-path P` (lands in "Queue / parked intake"), then `roadmap rate --issue-num N --rated P/S/A/E` — and promoted or removed later with `roadmap move`. Closed-issue drift is reported by `utils/pdda/pdda.sh issue-doc-sync` and fixed with `roadmap reconcile-state`. Enforced by `utils/pdda/pdda.sh roadmap-coverage`; governance lives in `PROJECT/PDDA.md`.
    60	- Do not create a second competing plan when a canonical `PROJECT/**` doc already exists.
    61	- Do not build a redundant solution when extending an existing one is viable (enforced by PDDA Phase 0 review). If >50% of the new solution overlaps with an existing one, the plan MUST include deprecating/deleting the old one.
    62	- SQLite has exactly two gateways, and they are **separate stores by design** — `src/rebalance/ingest/db/` opens this project's own index (path resolved from `REBALANCE_DB`), while `HiQS/hiqs/db.py` opens the HiQS clean-room rebuild's app-data store, staged to spin out to its own repo. They address different database files and are not converged (settled in GH-136, 2026-08-30). New SQLite access goes through one of them: a direct `sqlite3.connect` anywhere else is pinned by `utils/pdda/check_banned_imports.py --check` against `utils/pdda/sqlite_connect_baseline.json` and fails CI — additions *and* stale baselines both block.
    63	- **No script or LaunchAgent sprawl (GH-241)**: Do not create ad-hoc `.sh` or `.py` files in `scripts/` or `utils/`, and do not add new LaunchAgent plists. New CLI commands go to `src/rebalance/cli/`, MCP tools to `src/rebalance/mcp/`, and background workflows to the central orchestrator (`index_ops.py`). Enforced mechanically in CI by `python utils/pdda/check_script_inventory.py --check` against `utils/pdda/script_inventory_baseline.json` — scanning all `.py`, `.sh`, and `.swift` files under `scripts/` and `utils/`, plus `*.plist.template` files (excluding non-template `.plist` files and `SCHEDULER.md`). Governance checks and baselines live exclusively in `utils/pdda/check_*.py` and `utils/pdda/*_baseline.json`. Exemptions require a non-empty `SCRIPT-INVENTORY-OK: <reason>` pragma in the first 10 lines AND explicit registration in `script_inventory_baseline.json`'s `exemptions` list with operator review. Additions and stale baselines both block.
    64	- Do not override deterministic PDDA findings with prose.
    65	- Do not report a win you did not verify with `rebalance doctor`, `pytest tests/`, or the relevant PDDA check.
    66	
