     1	# CLIO
     2	
     3	A Claude Code skill that installs a `UserPromptSubmit` hook logging every prompt
     4	you submit — across every repo, on one machine — to a single centralized file:
     5	`~/.claude/prompt-log.jsonl`.
     6	
     7	Each line records a timestamp, repo name, git branch, machine name, session ID,
     8	and the prompt text (with auto-injected context like `<ide_selection>` blocks
     9	stripped out, so it's a record of what you actually typed).
    10	
    11	An optional second script converts that JSONL into human-readable Markdown —
    12	newest entry first — at any location you choose, such as a note in an Obsidian
    13	vault. It can run on demand or on a 5-minute `launchd` schedule (macOS).
    14	
    15	See [INSTALL.md](INSTALL.md) for the full install, verify, export, auto-sync, and
    16	uninstall instructions.
    17	
    18	## Why
    19	
    20	If you use Claude Code across many repos and machines, there's no built-in way
    21	to see everything you've asked it over time. This gives you one append-only
    22	log you can grep, sync to notes, or just keep as an audit trail.
    23	
    24	## Use cases
    25	
    26	- **Cross-device recall.** You work on the same project from a laptop and a
    27	  desktop (or any multiple-device setup) and want to answer "where/when did I
    28	  ask Claude to do X on this project?" without digging through separate
    29	  session histories per machine.
    30	- **Branch-level recall.** Each entry records the git branch checked out at
    31	  prompt time, so you can trace a specific ask back to the branch it happened
    32	  on — even after that branch is merged or deleted.
    33	- **Cross-project AI memory, layered into a "second brain."** Point the
    34	  Markdown export at an Obsidian vault and, once that vault is vectorized/
    35	  indexed for retrieval, an AI assistant can search across *what you asked
    36	  Claude Code to do*, alongside your other notes — one more layer in a
    37	  multi-layered personal knowledge system, not just a flat log file.
    38	
    39	## Requirements
    40	
    41	- macOS or Linux
    42	- [`jq`](https://jqlang.org/) (`brew install jq` / `apt install jq`)
    43	
    44	## License
    45	
    46	Apache License 2.0 — see [LICENSE](LICENSE).
    47	
    48	This project is provided **"AS IS," WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY
    49	KIND**, either express or implied (Apache 2.0 §7). It runs on your machine
    50	with a hook that shells out and edits your Claude Code `settings.json` —
    51	read the scripts before running them, and use at your own risk.

